# Copyright (c) 2026 Bjorn Pagen
# The checks of the lint preset, which runs clang-tidy on every translation
# unit and fails on any finding: bugs the compiler's warnings miss, and
# needless copies.
#
# A closed sum of ours is read by one fold, idr::match, which refuses a
# missing case at compile time; the readers that ask for one alternative
# and drop what they learned, std::visit's dispatch through function
# pointers above eleven alternatives, and TypeSwitch's ladder of casts are
# refused here, by qualified name, since visit is too common a word for a
# poisoned identifier. A moved reuse token's handle used again is
# bugprone-use-after-move's.
Checks: >-
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*
CheckOptions:
  bugprone-unsafe-functions.CustomFunctions: >-
    ^::std::(__[a-z0-9_]+::)?visit$,idr::match,dispatches through function pointers above eleven alternatives and checks no case;
    ^::std::(__[a-z0-9_]+::)?get_if$,idr::match,asks for one alternative and drops what it learned;
    ^::std::(__[a-z0-9_]+::)?holds_alternative$,idr::match,asks for one alternative and drops what it learned;
    ^::llvm::.*TypeSwitch.*::Case$,an interface or idr::match,is a ladder of casts
